{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'cat /workspace/TASK.md'","aggregated_output":"# Task: H12 — Ledger: grouped aggregation with deterministic projection\n\n> Held-out RFC-0005 suite · Shape: Collection/data transformation (2/2).\n> You are maintaining an **existing correct system**; do not rewrite it from\n> scratch. Change only what the task requires.\n\n## Base (workspace)\n\nThe workspace contains a correct, deterministic ledger module\n(`h12.ledger`). Entries have `category`, `amount`, and `valid`. The current\n`report` produces one `<category>:<sum>` line per category in **first-seen\norder** (valid entries only, no counts, no sorted projection). The program is\ndriven by the environment variable `H12_SCENARIO` and prints deterministic\nlines.\n\n## Required change\n\nChange `report` to a **grouped aggregation with a deterministic projection**:\n\n```text\n<category>:<count>:<sum>\n```\n\nRequirements:\n\n- only `valid` entries participate;\n- each category gets its own count and sum;\n- categories are emitted in **lexicographic order** (so the output is\n  deterministic regardless of input order);\n- an empty input (or no valid entries) produces exactly the fixed line\n  `EMPTY`;\n- negative amounts participate with their real value (they are not filtered);\n- multiple entries in the same category accumulate correctly.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe hidden verifier drives the compiled program through scenarios (including\npermuted input arrangements) and checks exact output lines: filtering,\nper-category count and sum, lexicographic projection, empty behavior,\nnegative amounts, and accumulation.\n\nThe workspace exposes only the program state and this task; the verifier is\nnot visible to you.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
